menu "EPM Drivers"

    config EPM_ACCEL_USE_STUB
        bool "Use synthetic accelerometer stub (no KX134 hardware)"
        default y
        help
            Selects components/epm_drivers/accel_stub.c as the hal_accel.h
            implementation instead of the real accel_kx134_spi.c driver.
            Default stays y until the real driver is confirmed against
            physical KX134 hardware (WHO_AM_I, at-rest g-values, zero
            dropped FIFO frames over a sustained run) -- see
            docs/decisions/ADR-017.

    config EPM_DISPLAY_USE_LEDC
        bool "Use plain-LEDC RGB LED (no WS2812/NeoPixel hardware)"
        default n
        help
            Selects components/epm_drivers/display_ledc.c as the hal_display.h
            implementation instead of the default WS2812 NeoPixel driver
            (display_neopixel.c). Kept as a Kconfig fallback for boards
            without an addressable RGB LED wired up -- see
            docs/decisions/ADR-016.

endmenu
